content.text:
Now game.js. Need to implement everything carefully.

Let me outline code:

```js
(function(){
 const D = window.GameData;
 const $ = (s,r=document)=>r.querySelector(s);
 const $$ = ...
 const app = $('#app');
 const screens = {title:..., cast:..., date:..., plan:..., heist:..., result:..., endings:...};
 let state = {...};
 let store = loadStore();
 let audio = ...
```

Store:
```js
function loadStore(){
 const def={endings:[],best:0,plays:0,sound:true};
 try{const raw=localStorage.getItem(D.STORE_KEY); if(raw){Object.assign(def, JSON.parse(raw));}}catch(e){}
 return def;
}
function saveStore(){try{localStorage.setItem(...)}catch(e){}}
```

Init:
- insert scene art into titleArt and sceneArt (maybe two instances of the SVG with duplicate gradient IDs!). Duplicate IDs can cause issues; but they're identical so the first will be referenced. However, when hidden, fine. Both use same IDs; browsers resolve `url(#skyG)` to the first occurrence in the document, which is title's. The second (date) will use the title's gradient definitions — those exist. Fine since same. But if the first is inside a hidden element, gradients still work. Yes.
Could instead use one scene and move it? No, fine.

Actually both scenes should have same svg; duplicate IDs are technically invalid but work. To be safe, generate a unique id suffix per scene instance? Modify scene(suffix) to append suffix to all ids. That requires refactoring art.js: use a suffix param and replace `id="skyG"` etc. Could do: `scene('a')` and replace `#skyG` references. Simpler: game only renders one full scene at a time by reusing same element? Title art and date art both need. I could render titleArt with scene and remove it when starting; date scene gets its own. Only one at a time in DOM if title art content is cleared on start? Then duplicate never exists simultaneously. But title screen might need art when returning. We can clear titleArt when leaving title and re-inject on return. Let's manage: on go('title'), if empty, inject. On go others, titleArt can stay; duplicates... Hmm.

Simplest robust: modify art.js scene function to accept prefix and use prefixed IDs for gradients, mask, filter. Then generate title with 't' and date with 'd'. Let me update art.js: wrap string with replacements? We can generate function `scene(prefix){prefix=prefix||'s'; let s = template...; return s.replace(/skyG/g, 'skyG'+prefix)...}` for all IDs referenced: skyG, sunGlow, riverG, bottomFade, wallG, softGlow, bridgeCut. Also any others? no. That handles. Let's patch after.

Game screens.

Title:
```js
$('#titleArt').innerHTML = Art.scene('t');
$('#sceneArt').innerHTML = Art.scene('d');
```
Both present; with prefixes unique. Good.

Update endingCount and sound label.

`startBtn` → Sound.click(); go('cast'); renderCast();

Cast:
renderCast builds cards. state.you etc initially null. When selecting:
```
state.you=id; state.partner=CHAR.partner;
const otherCouple = pairs[other couple]; state.o1=..., state.o2=...
renderCast(); // to update badges
updateCastNote();
$('#castNext').disabled=false;
```
Card heights: use Art.character.

Need to show pairing info clearly. Cards get badge:
- if you: "SEN"
- if partner: "RANDEVU"
- else: "DİĞER ÇİFT".

Note: pair can be computed by selecting couple. Selected char card. 

Cast note default when none. After selection show:
```
<div class="cast-note-icon" style="...">icon</div>
<div>
 <strong>{name} · {tag}</strong>
 <p>{perk} Randevun <b>{partner}</b>, diğer çift <b>{o1} & {o2}</b>.</p>
</div>
```
Trait description maybe.

Cast back → title.

Start date:
- reset stats: kimya = 35, ortaklik = 25 + (you==='kerem'?12:0), suphe=0.
- tokens base computed later.
- state.sceneIndex=0; go date; build castRow.
