content.text:
The `.heist-wrap` z-index is 3, above shade z1. Good. The overlay intro z20 above. Grain z60.

Another issue: `.dialog-ghost` uses `mask-image`; on Safari needs -webkit, included. Good.

Now the plan note HTML uses `state.suphe` from the date. Good.

Need to update the heist background night look? The scene is at dusk; the shade darkens it. Fine.

Now test result/caught. We need to restart the game to test updated balance. But before that, check the heist background visually with a reload + skip? We can navigate quickly by using JS to manipulate? The state isn't exposed. We'll play through again with the automated run, but let's improve the tester speed: add a debug query param? No. We can use the saved localStorage? No, gameplay state isn't saved.

We'll just replay. It takes ~10 interactions. Fine.

But first, finish the current run to see the result screen (it's already at round 4/5). Let it miss all; suspicion might not reach 100 under the old logic (the run started before reload? We haven't reloaded since the code changes!). The page is still running the old JS from before the changes. Need to reload to apply. So the current run is irrelevant.

Let's reload and play again. This time use the same path but faster. Then at the heist, we can purposely miss to test caught (with new balance). To speed the misses, click the gauge when outside the zone 5 times quickly. But between rounds there's a 1.25s pause. We can click every ~1.5s. We can script: wait for the round to be active by checking `#gaugeZone` opacity=1, then click at a spot likely outside the zone? The gauge click checks the needle angle, not the click position, so clicking anytime may hit if the needle is in the zone. To force a miss, we can wait until the needle is outside the zone; the probability is high (zone 30%). Or use the support? No.

We can read the needle angle and zone center, then click only when outside. Use page.evaluate to read the transform and zone dashoffset. Or just click repeatedly every 300ms during a round: the first click resolves (hit or miss) and locks; subsequent clicks do nothing until next round. Chance of hit ~30% each round; with 5 rounds, maybe 1-2 hits, suspicion still might reach 100. To guarantee all misses, we could use a small script:
```
async function missRound(page){
  await page.waitForFunction(()=>{ const z=document.querySelector('#gaugeZone'); return z && parseFloat(z.style.opacity)===1; });
  // compute zone center from style
  const info=await page.evaluate(()=>{...});
  // wait until needle outside: read current angle from transform; use waitForFunction with the zone data
  await page.waitForFunction(({c,h})=>{ ... }, {c,h}, {timeout:...});
  await page.locator('#gauge').click({position:{x:...}})
}
